From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 10:08:18 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 437/437] wifi: mt6797: advertise the scan SSIDs

0423 made the scan path accept SSIDs but left max_scan_ssids at zero, so
cfg80211 refused every active scan before it reached the driver. Advertise
the four the firmware's command carries.

Part of the Wi-Fi daily-use plan, phase 3.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c
index 4ed621a69..17c1c93c3 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c
@@ -2119,12 +2119,12 @@ static int mt6797_mac_register(struct device *dev, struct mt6797_hif *hif,
 	 * Normal profiles do not advertise this experimental ownership.
 	 */
 	ieee80211_hw_set(hw, CONNECTION_MONITOR);
-	hw->wiphy->max_scan_ssids = 0;
+	hw->wiphy->max_scan_ssids = MT6797_SCAN_SSIDS;
 	/* Userspace may attach elements to a scan request (the standard
 	 * supplicant always does); with a hw_scan operation mac80211 keeps a
 	 * zero limit, and cfg80211 would then reject every such request. The
-	 * one admitted scan is passive and transmits no probe request, so the
-	 * elements are accepted here and never read; mac80211 subtracts its own.
+	 * firmware builds its own probe requests, so the elements are accepted
+	 * here and never read; mac80211 subtracts its own.
 	 */
 	hw->wiphy->max_scan_ie_len = 256;
 	ieee80211_hw_set(hw, SIGNAL_DBM);
